          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="230" y="700"/><mxPoint x="800" y="700"/></Array></mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rules" value="&lt;b&gt;Rules.&lt;/b&gt; Change flows up only through watchers: a command writes a file and forgets, so a change from MO2 and one from Modbench are the same signal. The Instance is derived from disk and nothing else; it recomputes whole (0.07 s for 764 mods), keeps its last value on a parse failure, and validates on activation and Refresh through the same path. Outside three per-release tables (game paths, implicit master names, the load-order file destination) no extension file names a game; a source scan holds it. Mods, Downloads and Toolbox never see a record." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="715" width="1140" height="60" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
